load @term/seed/code/structure/space/vector
  find vector-space

# An antivector: a grade just below the top of a geometric algebra, the dual of a vector, an oriented hyperplane rather
# than an oriented line. In three dimensions an antivector is a bivector (a plane), which is why the cross product (a
# plane) masquerades as a vector there. The form carries the underlying vector space.
form antivector
  link space, like vector-space
